"color:red\">0</span> | - |\r\n| distance | 2246 | 468 | 1196 | - |\r\n\r\n\r\n*prompt 2*\r\n| | Gemini 2.5 Pro | GPT-5 | GPT-5 mini | Claude Sonnet 4.5 |\r\n|:---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\r\n| continent | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> |\r\n| country | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> |\r\n| city/ town | <span style=\"color:red\">0</span> | <span style=\"color:red\">0</span> | <span style=\"color:red\">0</span> | <span style=\"color:red\">0</span> |\r\n| distance | 2411 | 2317 | 484 | 1652 |\r\n\r\n\r\n*prompt 3*\r\n| | Gemini 2.5 Pro | GPT-5 | GPT-5 mini | Claude Sonnet 4.5 |\r\n|:---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\r\n| continent | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> |\r\n| country | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> | <span style=\"color:green\">1</span> |\r\n| city/ town | <span style=\"color:red\">0</span> | <span style=\"color:red\">0</span> | <span style=\"color:red\">0</span> | <span style=\"color:red\">0</span> |\r\n| distance | 1765 | 2429 | 2480 | 1624 |\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n<br/><br/>\r\n\r\n\r\n**Podsumowanie**\r\nŚrednia pomyłka w kilometrach w zależności od prompta dla poszczególnych modeli\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n| Prompt     | Gemini 2.5 Pro | GPT-5 | GPT-5 mini | Claude Sonnet 4.5 |\r\n|-------------|----------------|--------|-------------|-------------------|\r\n| prompt 1    | 694            | 215    | 2517        | -                 |\r\n| prompt 2    | 717            | 643    | 409         | 2681              |\r\n| prompt 3    | 465            | 687    | 1371        | 2474              |\r\n\r\n\r\n## Właściwe testy wybranych modeli\r\n\r\n\r\nPrzeprowadziliśmy testy wszystkich wcześniej ocenianych modeli na pełnym zestawie danych obejmującym 45 zdjęć. Dodatkowo wykonaliśmy analogiczne testy dla dedykowanego modelu geolokalizacyjnego GeoCLIP.\r\n\r\nNa podstawie współrzędnych otrzymanych w wynikach estymacji geolokalizacji modelu GeoCLIP chcieliśmy mieć również te dane, które zwracały pozostałe modele: kontynent, państwo, miasto. Wykorzystaliśmy bibliotekę `geopy` i jej metodę `geolocator.reverse`\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n  <summary><strong>Kod</strong></summary>\r\n\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# --- 1. Installation ---\r\n!pip install pandas geopy\r\n\r\n\r\n# --- 2. Imports and Google Drive Mount ---\r\nfrom google.colab import drive, files\r\nfrom geopy.geocoders import Nominatim\r\nfrom tqdm.notebook import tqdm\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\nimport os\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n# Mount Google Drive to access your files\r\ndrive.mount('/content/drive')\r\n\r\n\r\n# --- 3. Define the File Path ---\r\n# *** Replace this path with the actual path to your CSV or Excel file on Google Drive ***\r\n# Example: /content/drive/MyDrive/MyProjectFolder/Image_Coordinates.xlsx\r\nfile_path = '/content/drive/MyDrive/geo-data/geo-dataset.xlsx'\r\n\r\n\r\n# --- 4. Load the Data ---\r\ntry:\r\n    if file_path.endswith('.csv'):\r\n        df = pd.read_csv(file_path)\r\n    elif file_path.endswith(('.xls', '.xlsx')):\r\n        df = pd.read_excel(file_path)\r\n    else:\r\n        print(\"Unsupported file type. Please use .csv or .xlsx.\")\r\n        exit()\r\n\r\n\r\n    print(f\"Successfully loaded {len(df)} records from the spreadsheet.\")\r\n    print(\"\\nFirst 5 rows of the loaded data:\")\r\n    # Display the column names to confirm they were loaded correctly\r\n    print(df.head())\r\n\r\n\r\nexcept Exception as e:\r\n    print(f\"Error loading file: {e}\")\r\n    print(\"Please double-check the 'file_path' and ensure your file is in Google Drive.\")\r\n    exit()\r\n\r\n\r\n# --- 5. Verify and Prepare Columns ---\r\n# *** ADJUST THESE COLUMN NAMES based on your spreadsheet ***\r\nLATITUDE_COL = 'Latitude'  # e.g., 'Actual Lat', 'Point 1 Lat'\r\nLONGITUDE_COL = 'Longitude' # e.g., 'Actual Lon', 'Point 1 Lon'\r\n\r\n\r\nif LATITUDE_COL not in df.columns or LONGITUDE_COL not in df.columns:\r\n    print(\"\\nERROR: Coordinate columns not found. Please adjust 'LATITUDE_COL' and 'LONGITUDE_COL' names.\")\r\n    print(\"Available columns:\", df.columns.tolist())\r\n    exit()\r\n\r\n\r\n# Extract coordinates as a list of tuples\r\ncoords_to_geocode = list(zip(df[LATITUDE_COL].astype(float), df[LONGITUDE_COL].astype(float)))\r\n\r\n\r\n# --- 6. Initialize Geocoder ---\r\ngeolocator = Nominatim(user_agent=\"CoordinateAnalyzer\")\r\ngeocoded_results = []\r\n\r\n\r\n# --- 7. Perform Reverse Geocoding Lookup ---\r\nfor lat, lon in tqdm(coords_to_geocode, desc=\"Reverse Geocoding\"):\r\n    location_str = f\"{lat}, {lon}\"\r\n\r\n\r\n    # Use a try-except block to handle occasional connection or service errors\r\n    try:\r\n        # Request the closest address for the coordinate\r\n        location = geolocator.reverse(location_str, exactly_one=True, timeout=10, language='en')\r\n    except Exception:\r\n        location = None\r\n\r\n\r\n    result = {\r\n        'Latitude': lat,\r\n        'Longitude': lon,\r\n        'Country': 'N/A',\r\n        'City/Town': 'N/A',\r\n        'Continent': 'N/A', # Cannot reliably determine continent from all geocoders\r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\n    if location:\r\n        address = location.raw.get('address', {})\r\n\r\n\r\n        # Extract City/Town (using multiple possible keys for robustness)\r\n        city = address.get('city') or address.get('town') or address.get('village')\r\n\r\n\r\n        result['Country'] = address.get('country', 'N/A')\r\n        result['City/Town'] = city if city else 'N/A'\r\n\r\n\r\n        # Determine Continent (Simple lookup - can be inaccurate for border cases)\r\n        # Note: Continent is often determined by mapping country name to a fixed list,\r\n        # but we'll use a simplified check here.\r\n        if 'Europe' in address.get('state_district', ''): # Very basic check\r\n             result['Continent'] = 'Europe'\r\n\r\n\r\n        # Optional: Add the full address for reference\r\n        result['Full Address'] = location.address\r\n\r\n\r\n    geocoded_results.append(result)\r\n\r\n\r\n# --- 8. Combine and Display Results ---\r\n# Create a DataFrame from the geocoded results\r\ndf_geocoded = pd.DataFrame(geocoded_results)\r\n\r\n\r\n# Combine the original dataframe with the new geocoded data\r\ndf_final = pd.concat([df.reset_index(drop=True), df_geocoded[['Country', 'City/Town', 'Continent', 'Full Address']]], axis=1)\r\n\r\n\r\nprint(\"\\n--- Final Geocoding Report ---\")\r\n# Display the table showing the new columns\r\ndf_output = df_final[['Latitude', 'Longitude', 'Country', 'City/Town', 'Continent']].head(10)\r\nprint(df_output.to_markdown(index=False))\r\n\r\n\r\n# Optional: Save the enhanced data back to Drive\r\noutput_file_path = '/content/drive/MyDrive/geo-data/Image_Coordinates_Geocoded.csv'\r\ndf_final.to_csv(output_file_path, index=False)\r\nprint(f\"\\nSaved full report to: {output_file_path}\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Wyniki\r\n\r\n\r\n* **Claude Sonnet 4.5**\r\n\r\n  <details>\r\n  <summary><strong>Wyniki</strong></summary>\r\n\r\n  | Filename | Difficulty | Coordinates | Continent | Country | City/Town | Distance (km) |\r\n  |-----------|-------------|-------------|------------|-----------|-------------|---------------|\r\n  | geo_1 | Easy | 46.0569, 14.5058 | Europe | Slovenia | Ljubljana | 600.26 |\r\n  | geo_2 | Easy | 48.8833, 2.3500 | Europe | France | Paris | 1.82 |\r\n  | geo_3 | Hard | 44.5, 28.0 | Europe | Romania | Dobrogea Region | 846.62 |\r\n  | geo_4 | Hard | 61.9117, 6.7194 | Europe | Norway | Stryn | 148.53 |\r\n  | geo_5 | Hard | 43.32, 21.90 | Europe | Serbia | Niš | 133.85 |\r\n  | geo_6 | Easy | 9.0765, 7.3986 | Afric