ch.\r\n\r\nOpiekun kierunku: dr inż. Michał Wągrowski\r\n\r\n[Zobacz pełny opis kierunku](#)\r\n\r\nProgram ustalony Uchwałą Senatu nr 110/2019 z dnia 26 czerwca 2019 r., zmieniony Uchwałą Senatu nr 91/2020 z dnia 8 maja 2020 r., zmieniony Uchwałą Senatu nr 7/2021 z dnia 3 marca 2021 r., zmieniony Uchwałą Senatu nr 19/2022 z dnia 2 marca 2022 r., zmieniony Uchwałą Senatu nr 5/2023 z dnia 1 lutego 2023 r. oraz Uchwałą nr 5/2024 Senatu AGH z dnia 24 stycznia 2024 r.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Praca naukowa:\r\n![obraz](/uploads/a64151fb64db4f95315832f2124820e4/obraz.png)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAccess Point\r\n\r\nClient\r\n→ Connection\r\nPower-Save (Sleep=True)\r\nWake-Up (Sleep=False)\r\nData\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFigure 1: Power-saving mechanisms enable a client station to enter power-save mode. Until the client wakes up, the access point will queue all bufferable frames destined for the client.\r\n\r\nThis complicates the analysis of systems since every layer must be carefully inspected, which is non-trivial because the behavior of one layer may influence the security of another.\r\n\r\nCoordinated Disclosure\r\nWe disclosed all identified vulnerabilities to the affected vendors. An overview and timeline of the disclosure process is available on our public repository.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBackground\r\nIn this section, we provide an overview of the power-saving mechanism and Wi-Fi Management Frame Protection (MFP).\r\n\r\n#### 2.1 Wi-Fi Power-Saving Mechanisms\r\nPower-save mechanisms have been part of the IEEE 802.11 standard since its first release in 1997. With the introduction of the IEEE 802.11e amendment, defining Quality-of-Service (QoS) enhancements for wireless LAN networks, the standard adopted more advanced power-save mechanisms [23, §11.2].\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 3. Latex\r\n![obraz](/uploads/885c5ca76c6b610da8402ec6aba264d2/obraz.png)\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nTHE POWER FUNCTION\r\n43\r\n\r\n... and the rule is proved that\r\n\r\n[ \\frac{d u^n}{d x} = n u^{n-1} \\frac{d u}{d x} ]\r\n\r\n\r\nwhere ( n ) is a positive fraction whose numerator and denominator are integers. This rule has already been used in the solution of numerous exercises.\r\n\r\nThe Derivative of a Constant\r\nLet ( y = c ), where ( c ) is a constant. Corresponding to any ( \\Delta x ), ( \\Delta y = 0 ), and consequently\r\n[ \\frac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x} = 0, ]\r\nand\r\n[ \\lim_{\\Delta x \\to 0} \\frac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x} = 0, ]\r\nor\r\n[ \\frac{d y}{d x} = 0. ]\r\n\r\nThe derivative of a constant is zero.\r\nInterpret this result geometrically.\r\n\r\nThe Derivative of the Sum of Two Functions\r\nLet\r\n[ y = u + v, ]\r\n\r\nwhere ( u ) and ( v ) are functions of ( x ). Let ( \\Delta u ), ( \\Delta v ), and ( \\Delta y ) be the increments of ( u ), ( v ), and ( y ), respectively, corresponding to the increment ( \\Delta x ):\r\n[ y + \\Delta y = u + \\Delta u + v + \\Delta v, ]\r\n[ \\Delta y = \\Delta u + \\Delta v, ]\r\n[ \\frac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x} = \\frac{\\Delta u}{\\Delta x} + \\frac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta x}, ]\r\n[ \\frac{d y}{d x} = \\frac{d u}{d x} + \\frac{d v}{d x}. ]\r\n\r\nThe derivative of the sum of two functions is equal to the sum of their derivatives.\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Po ostawieniu Latex rendering na równaniach:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe Power Function\r\n==================\r\n\r\n... and the rule is proved that\r\n\r\n```math\r\n\\frac{d u^n}{d x} = n u^{n-1} \\frac{d u}{d x}\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhere \\(n\\) is a positive fraction whose numerator and denominator are integers. This rule has already been used in the solution of numerous exercises.\r\n\r\nThe Derivative of a Constant\r\n=============================\r\n\r\nLet \\(y = c\\), where \\(c\\) is a constant. Corresponding to any \\(\\Delta x\\), \\(\\Delta y = 0\\), and consequently\r\n\r\n```math\r\n\\frac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x} = 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nand\r\n\r\n```math\r\n\\lim_{\\Delta x \\to 0} \\frac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x} = 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nor\r\n\r\n```math\r\n\\frac{d y}{d x} = 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe derivative of a constant is zero.  \r\nInterpret this result geometrically.\r\n\r\nThe Derivative of the Sum of Two Functions\r\n==========================================\r\n\r\nLet\r\n\r\n```math\r\ny = u + v\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhere \\(u\\) and \\(v\\) are functions of \\(x\\). Let \\(\\Delta u\\), \\(\\Delta v\\), and \\(\\Delta y\\) be the increments of \\(u\\), \\(v\\), and \\(y\\), respectively, corresponding to the increment \\(\\Delta x\\):\r\n\r\n```math\r\ny + \\Delta y = u + \\Delta u + v + \\Delta v\r\n```\r\n\r\n```math\r\n\\Delta y = \\Delta u + \\Delta v\r\n```\r\n\r\n```math\r\n\\frac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x} = \\frac{\\Delta u}{\\Delta x} + \\frac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta x}\r\n```\r\n\r\n```math\r\n\\frac{d y}{d x} = \\frac{d u}{d x} + \\frac{d v}{d x}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe derivative of the sum of two functions is equal to the sum of their derivatives.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Wnioski:\r\n\r\nGPT-4 OCR radzi sobie wyjątkowo dobrze z przetwarzaniem prac naukowych, które wykorzystują LaTeX. System skutecznie odczytuje teksty o wysokiej jakości i poprawnie rekonstruuje zapis LaTeX, co zapewnia wysoką dokładność w odwzorowywaniu matematycznych wzorów i formuł. Choć GPT-4 OCR nie jest w stanie odtworzyć wykresów, charakteryzuje się bardzo niskim wskaźnikiem błędów **(Word error rate)** w przypadku tekstów wyraźnych i dobrze sformatowanych. Testy na dokumentach o niższej jakości pozostają do zrobienia.\r\n\r\n\r\n# Donut 🍩 demonstration, hugging face\r\n\r\n## Input:\r\n\r\n![image](/uploads/38b51be3ce1069fba43cbf125cc0d42c/image.png)\r\n\r\n## Output:\r\n\r\n\\[ { \r\n\r\n\"cnt\": \"7 Kel \\<s_cnt\\> 7 Kel \\<s_cnt\\> 311\",\r\n\r\n \"price\": \"2101\"\r\n\r\n } \\]\r\n\r\n## Input:\r\n\r\n![image](/uploads/dcd5602a729eb3f313338ae57c4ab6e5/image.png)\r\n\r\n## Output:\r\n\r\n![image.png](/uploads/10e881a8fa7c2ea7213824c8225ec0d1/image.png){width=550 height=226}\r\n\r\n## Input:\r\n\r\n![image](/uploads/59b9d52efd267adb297218019c70e236/image.png)\r\n\r\n## Output:\r\n\r\n![image.png](/uploads/c302e344281050c9dcfcb8c292d32ead/image.png){width=357 height=395}\r\n\r\n### Czy Donut jest użyteczny?\r\n\r\nNależy wziąć pod uwagę że Donut należy najpierw przetrenować na odpowiedniej bazie wejściowej daje spore możliwości do niszowych i wyspecjalizowanych zastosowań. Niestety ciężko jest znaleźć model w ogólnej wersji przetrenowanej na sporym zbiorze wejściowym. Twórcy załączyli kilka wersji demonstracyjnych ale żadnego w obszerniejszej wersji.\r\n\r\n\r\n# Limity GPT-4o pod czytania danych i formatowania markdown:\r\n\r\n## 1. Zdjęcie kartki z rozbudowaną tabelą\r\n![472373270_983339440363865_299861283044485903_n](/uploads/9883ff2c9d6372a145724687bc251310/472373270_983339440363865_299861283044485903_n.jpg)\r\n\r\n### Wynik:\r\n\r\n# NetworkProGuide  \r\n## CIDR/IPv4 Cheat Sheet  \r\n\r\n### Subnets  \r\n\r\n| CIDR     | Subnet Mask     | # of Addresses | Wildcard          | Classful Ranges                     |\r\n|----------|-----------------|----------------|-------------------|-------------------------------------|\r\n| /0       | 0.0.0.0         | 4,294,967,296  | 255.255.255.255   | A 0.0.0.0 - 127.255.255.255        |\r\n| /1       | 128.0.0.0       | 2,147,483,648  | 127.255.255.255   | B 128.0.0.0 - 191.255.255.255      |\r\n| /2       | 192.0.0.0       | 1,073,741,824  | 63.255.255.255    | C 192.0.0.0 - 223.255.255.255      |\r\n| /3       | 224.0.0.0       | 536,870,912    | 31.255.255.255    | D 224.0.0.0 - 239.255.255.255      |\r\n| /4       | 240.0.0.0       | 268,435,456    | 15.255.255.255    | E 240.0.0.0 - 255.255.255.255      |\r\n| /5       | 248.0.0.0       | 134,217,728    | 7.255.255.255     |                                     |\r\n| /6       | 252.0.0.0       | 67,108,864     | 3.255.255.255     |                                     |\r\n| /7       | 254.0.0.0       | 33,554,432     | 1.255.255.255     |                                     |\r\n| /8       | 255.0.0.0       | 16,777,216     | 0.255.255.255     |      